==Ingredients==

* 3 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] cranberry or pinto beans
* 1 cup [[Cookbook:Spelt|spelt]] or [[Cookbook:Wheat|wheat berries]] (available at gourmet-food shops)
* ¼ cup extra-virgin [[Cookbook:Olive Oil|olive oil]], plus more for drizzling
* ½ [[Cookbook:Pound|pound]] sweet Italian [[Cookbook:Sausage|sausage]], casings removed
* 1 pound [[Cookbook:Kale|kale]], preferably Tuscan, coarse stems removed, cut into thick ribbons
* 1 medium-large [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]]
* 1 large [[Cookbook:Carrot|carrot]], peeled and diced
* 1 large rib [[Cookbook:Celery|celery]], trimmed and diced
* 3 [[Cookbook:Garlic|cloves garlic]], thinly [[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]]
* 5 cups homemade [[Cookbook:Chicken|chicken]] [[Cookbook:Stock|stock]], or canned low-sodium stock, plus more if needed
* 1 cup peeled, seeded, and diced [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]], or drained canned diced tomatoes
* 1 sprig fresh [[Cookbook:Rosemary|rosemary]]
* 1 sprig fresh [[Cookbook:Sage|sage]]
* [[Cookbook:Salt|Sea salt]] and freshly ground [[Cookbook:Pepper|pepper]]
* ½ cup freshly grated [[Cookbook:Cheese|Parmigiano-Reggiano cheese]]

==Procedure==

# [[Cookbook:Soaking Beans|Soak]] beans and spelt overnight in separate bowls of cold water.
# Drain and set aside.
# Heat olive oil in a large pot over medium-high heat.
# Add sausage.
# Cook stirring occasionally, until meat begins to separate and brown (3–5 minutes).
# Stir in kale, onion, carrot, celery, and garlic.
# Cook until softened (about 10 minutes).
# Add beans, spelt, chicken stock, and tomatoes.
# Bring to [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]].
# Stir in rosemary and sage.
# Reduce heat.
# [[Cookbook:Simmering|Simmer]] mixture for 60–70 minutes, until beans are tender; if soup is too thick, add chicken stock.
# Season to taste with salt and pepper.
# [[Cookbook:Ladle|Ladle]] soup into bowls.
# Drizzle with olive oil, and sprinkle on cheese.
# Serve immediately.

==Notes, tips, and variations==

* Have this soup first with bread, like [[Cookbook:Ciabatta|ciabatta]], then finish with some cold cuts, like [[Cookbook:Salami|salami]] and [[Cookbook:Prosciutto|prosciutto]].
* Instead of using spelt, you can substitute [[Cookbook:Barley|barley]].
* If you can't find Tuscan kale, you can use regular kale, [[Cookbook:Mustard Greens|mustard greens]], or [[Cookbook:Swiss Chard|Swiss chard]].
* This soup tastes even better the next day.

